#. Tag: title
#: storeprint.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "Detailed Guides: Document Creation, Storage, and Printing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section of the documentation will cover everything you need to know "
"about starting a new document, saving a document, retrieving a saved "
"document and printing a document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: storeprint.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid "Beginning a New Document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: storeprint.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid "create new document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid "Starting a new document can be done 5 ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can <link linkend=\"starting-kword\">start &kword; from the &kde; Panel</"
"link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can <link linkend=\"starting-kword\">start &kword; from the command "
"line</link> by typing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: storeprint.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid "<prompt>$</prompt><userinput><command>kword &amp;</command></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can begin a new document in &kword; by selecting <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>New</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the "
"menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use the keyboard shortcut: <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;"
"<keycap>N</keycap></keycombo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"or by clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"filenew2."
"png\" format=\"PNG\" align=\"center\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> on "
"the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid "However you begin a new document, a dialog box appears:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid "This dialog box allows you to:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: storeprint.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid "Start a new document from a template"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: storeprint.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open an existing document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: storeprint.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open a recent document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; remembers your previous choice. That previous choice will be the "
"current default option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: storeprint.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "Starting a new document from a template"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to start a new document based on a template, you must first choose "
"which template you want to use."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use the icons located along the left edge of the dialog box to select your "
"template group. Simply click with the &LMB; to select that group and display "
"all the available templates of that group."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Remember templates are either Text Oriented (Blank Document) or Page Layout "
"templates. If you need to review the differences, click <link linkend=\"wp-"
"vs-dtp\">here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you have selected the icon, you are shown all the available templates, "
"each with a title and a small icon which shows you the general layout of the "
"template."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; comes with four standard template groups. You can add new icons by "
"installing outside templates, or <link linkend=\"template-creation"
"\">creating templates of your own</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To select your template, click on it with the &LMB;. The selected template "
"will be highlighted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Confirm your choice by clicking the <guibutton>Use This Template</guibutton> "
"button. This will begin a new document with that template."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For faster access to a template, simply double click on the template, and "
"&kword; will immediately load that template."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: storeprint.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid "Opening an existing document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the <guibutton>Open Existing Document...</guibutton> button, and an "
"new dialog box is revealed. For more details on this dialog box refer to "
"<link linkend=\"file-dialog\">Using the file selection dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: storeprint.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open a Recent Document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; keeps track of the most recently edited documents. You can select "
"one of these documents by clicking on the icon labeled <guilabel>Recent "
"Documents</guilabel>. This will list the most recently edited files on the "
"system. Simply click on the icon of the desired file with the &LMB; and "
"click <guibutton>Open This Document</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: storeprint.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "Saving a Document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: storeprint.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid "saving a document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you have entered text and data into a document, you will usually want "
"to save this to a file on your hard drive."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; can create a <literal role=\"extension\">.pdf</literal> file for "
"you. For instructions see <link linkend=\"qd-pdf\">How do I create a "
"<literal role=\"extension\">.pdf</literal> file?</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: storeprint.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenuitem>Save</guimenuitem> Command"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenuitem>Save</guimenuitem> command can be invoked 3 ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Save</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the Menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use the keyboard shortcut: <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;"
"<keycap>S</keycap></keycombo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"or by clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref="
"\"filefloppy.png\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> on the "
"toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:171 storeprint.docbook:339
#, no-c-format
msgid "Any of these methods results in the same action by &kword;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting the <guimenuitem>Save</guimenuitem> command, you are "
"instructing &kword; to save the file under the current filename. You will "
"not be given the option to change the filename or its location. If you want "
"to change the name of the file, or where it is saved, you must select <link "
"linkend=\"command-save-as\"><menuchoice> <guimenu>File</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Save As...</guimenuitem></menuchoice></link> from the "
"Menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have not saved this file before, it does not have a filename. &kword; "
"automatically executes the <link linkend=\"command-save-as"
"\"><guimenuitem>Save As...</guimenuitem></link> command so you can provide a "
"file name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; does not report a successful save. Therefore, if the file was saved "
"without incident, &kword; will return you to editing your document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can verify that the file was saved, by checking the titlebar. If there "
"are unsaved changes, the titlebar will have <emphasis>[modified]</emphasis> "
"in the titlebar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the save was successful, only the filename will be in the titlebar. If "
"there is a problem with the save, an error box will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: storeprint.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenuitem>Save As...</guimenuitem> Command"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: storeprint.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid "saving a document with new name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: storeprint.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid "General"
msgstr "General"

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenuitem>Save As...</guimenuitem> command can be invoked 2 ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Save As...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the Menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"or by trying to <guimenuitem>Save</guimenuitem> a file which does not yet "
"have a filename."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The difference between the <guimenuitem>Save</guimenuitem> and the "
"<guimenuitem>Save As...</guimenuitem> command, is the <guimenuitem>Save As..."
"</guimenuitem> command prompts you for a filename, and lets you select a "
"different file format or location. The <guimenuitem>Save</guimenuitem> "
"command simply saves the file in the previous location."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: storeprint.docbook:244 storeprint.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the dialog box"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid "When you select <guimenuitem>Save As...</guimenuitem> a dialog appears."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:255
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information on using this dialog, see the section entitled <link "
"linkend=\"file-dialog\">Using the file selection dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:258
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you are in the folder you want to save the file in, type a filename "
"into the <guilabel>Location:</guilabel> box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; can create a <literal role=\"extension\">.pdf</literal> file for "
"you. For instructions see <link linkend=\"qd-pdf\">How do I create a "
"<literal role=\"extension\">.pdf</literal> file</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:263
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is no need to put a <literal role=\"extension\">.kwd</literal> at the "
"end of your filename, &kword; will do this for you."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:268
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&UNIX; filenames are more flexible than many other operating systems. "
"Filenames can:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:272
#, no-c-format
msgid "be of nearly any length"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:273
#, no-c-format
msgid "be any combination of upper and lowercase letters"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:274
#, no-c-format
msgid "include spaces and punctuation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid "Filenames should not:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:281
#, no-c-format
msgid "begin with a space or period"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"end with a common file extension (<literal role=\"extension\">.ps</literal>,"
"<literal role=\"extension\">.pdf</literal>,etc)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:289
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you have entered the correct information you can click on "
"<guibutton>Save</guibutton> to complete the save."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; does not report a successful save. Therefore, if the file was saved "
"without incident, &kword; will return you to editing your document. If there "
"is a problem with the save, an error box will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:298
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; will only allow you to save your file where you are allowed to by "
"the permissions listed by the operating system. If you try to save outside "
"that area, &kword; will report an error."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: storeprint.docbook:308
#, no-c-format
msgid "Retrieving a Saved Document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: storeprint.docbook:309
#, no-c-format
msgid "loading a &kword; file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:310
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenuitem>Open...</guimenuitem> command can be invoked 4 ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By clicking the <guilabel>Open Existing Document</guilabel> tab when <link "
"linkend=\"new-doc\">Opening a New Document</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Open...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:328
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use the keyboard shortcut: <keycombo>&Ctrl;<keycap>O</keycap></"
"keycombo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:333
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"or by clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"fileopen."
"png\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> on the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:342
#, no-c-format
msgid "When trying to open a file, a dialog appears."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:351
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information on using this dialog, see the section entitled <link "
"linkend=\"file-dialog\">Using the file dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use this dialog to locate the document you want to load. Once located, click "
"once with the &LMB; on the filename. Once the filename is selected click "
"<guibutton>OK</guibutton>. The file will be loaded."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is a <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> button, if you click this button, "
"the load will be aborted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: storeprint.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid "Printing A Document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: storeprint.docbook:364
#, no-c-format
msgid "printing a document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenuitem>Print...</guimenuitem> command can be invoked 3 ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:369
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Print...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use the keyboard shortcut: <keycombo>&Ctrl;<keycap>P</keycap></"
"keycombo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:378
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"or by clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref="
"\"fileprint.png\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> on the "
"toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:384
#, no-c-format
msgid "No matter how you do this, the &kde; print dialog will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The top combo box labeled <guilabel>Name:</guilabel> shows the currently "
"selected printer. To configure this printer click on the "
"<guibutton>Properties</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:398
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To select a different printer, click on the combo box and select the desired "
"printer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:401
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to print your output into a postscript file, to a PDF file, a "
"fax modem (to send it as a fax) or email the file as a PDF file, select the "
"appropriate option from the combo box labeled <guilabel>Name</guilabel>. "
"Once that option has been selected, enter the filename into the text box "
"labeled <guilabel>Output file:</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:406
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The line labeled <guilabel>State</guilabel> tells you if your printer is "
"currently connected and if it is printing another page. You can not change "
"any information on this line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:408
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The lines labeled <guilabel>Type</guilabel> and <guilabel>Location</"
"guilabel> tells you what type of printer is currently selected and where "
"that printer is located. You can not change any information on these lines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:412
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The line labeled <guilabel>Comment</guilabel> describes how &kword; "
"interacts with your computer (what driver and print system it is using). You "
"can not change anything on this line. Complete setup of the &kde; printing "
"system is beyond the scope of this document. For more information see the "
"&kde; print web site at <ulink url=\"http://printing.kde.org\">http://"
"printing.kde.org</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to print all pages of your document and only one copy, you can "
"click <guibutton>Print</guibutton>. If you want to change the number of "
"copies or only print selected pages, click the <guibutton>Options &gt;&gt;</"
"guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:421
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>System Options</guibutton> button allows a user to change the "
"setup of the printers and &kde; print system. This is also beyond the scope "
"of this manual. If you need to make changes please refer to the &kde; print "
"web site at <ulink url=\"http://printing.kde.org\">http://printing.kde.org</"
"ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:424
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Depending on which printing system your computer uses, you may find that you "
"have more printing options then those described below. What is described "
"here, is available on <emphasis>most</emphasis> systems."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:428
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you click <guibutton>Options &gt;&gt;</guibutton>, the dialog box "
"changes to:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:437
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Under <guilabel>Page Selection</guilabel>, you can select either to print "
"the whole document (select <guilabel>All</guilabel>), print the page the "
"cursor is located on (simply select <guilabel>Current</guilabel>), or print "
"a range of pages. If you select the <guilabel>Range</guilabel> option, enter "
"your page range in the text box provided. (Example: 3-13)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:443
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the combo box labeled <guilabel>Page set:</guilabel> you can tell &kword; "
"to print the <guilabel>Even Pages</guilabel>, the <guilabel>Odd Pages</"
"guilabel> or <guilabel>All Pages</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:447
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the box on the right labeled <guilabel>Copies:</guilabel>, you should set "
"the number of copies you want printed. You can either enter the number "
"directly into the box, or use the arrows to adjust the number. &kword; can "
"print a maximum of 999 copies at once."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:452
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can have &kde; collate your documents by clicking on the "
"<guilabel>Collate</guilabel> check box. If selected, &kde; will print all of "
"the pages for copy 1, then print all the pages for copy 2, &etc; If not "
"selected, &kde; will print all of the copies of the first page, then all of "
"the copies of the second page, &etc;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:458
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also determine if the document is printed in forward order (print "
"first page first), or reverse order (print last page first)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:462
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you click on <guibutton>Options &lt;&lt;</guibutton>, the print dialog "
"will compress down to the previous view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:465
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Depending on your systems setup, you may have additional options available "
"to you. These options are discussed at <ulink url=\"http://printing.kde.org"
"\">http://printing.kde.org</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:467
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you are satisfied with your selections, you can click <guibutton>OK</"
"guibutton> to print."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: storeprint.docbook:470
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you click on <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton>, the printing will be aborted."
msgstr ""

